          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"undset-kristin-lavransdatter-0b1f0b873e3287c7\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.98,\"analysis\":\"The imagined words are a retrospective avowal of Simon’s enduring love for Kristin. They present his long-maintained emotional state as true, without undertaking a new relational commitment. Because Simon deliberately plans and mentally rehearses the disclosure, the passage supplies no independent expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The words are projected rather than actually spoken at this point, but quotation status does not alter their clear truth-conditional force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"imagined\",\"description\":\"Simon silently formulates what he intends to tell Kristin before dying: “Jeg har elsket dig i alle disse aarene”; he does not utter it in this scene.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Simon, gravely ill and believing death near, contemplates revealing the love he has concealed for years from Kristin, his former betrothed and now his wife’s sister. The disclosure is carefully considered: he reasons that it cannot make Kristin more sorrowful and resolves to say it once before death. This deliberation makes the core event a planned avowal rather than an affect-driven verbal discharge. The wider supplied passage later confirms that he never delivers this intended declaration, instead addressing reconciliation and family obligations.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Han vilde si hende det, før han døde — en eneste gang: Jeg har elsket dig i alle disse aarene —.”\",\"supports\":\"The phrase is an imagined future disclosure and explicitly avows love extending across many years, strongly supporting T and the imagined status.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“for den saks skyld kunde han godt si hende om den. Det kunde umulig gjøre hende mere tungsindig.”\",\"supports\":\"Simon weighs the likely effect of disclosure before deciding to speak, indicating deliberate planning rather than expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Later, Simon reflects: “Det var ikke det som han hadde ment at si hende. Men han hadde ikke kunnet tale anderledes.”\",\"supports\":\"The wider supplied context confirms that the rehearsed love declaration remained an unrealized intention rather than an actual direct utterance.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked as affirmative perfect form and retained as a valid explicit I-love-you instance.\",\"supports\":\"Supports reading the highlighted wording as a retrospective love avowal rather than a nonsemantic or merely formal use.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core force as a deliberate avowal of a longstanding emotional state. Neither commitment-taking P, independently expressive/reflexive E, nor residual O is needed.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The continuation “i alle disse aarene” is essential context for the perfect form: Simon means that his love has persisted over many years.\"}"
        }
      ],
